+/// and the log), the records and the series behind them, how many (segment, series) pairs the sidecars
+/// were written for, and what each query read. It knows nothing about money — a store cannot measure a
+/// price — which is why the comparison this type feeds is about bytes.
+#[derive(Debug, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
